1
00:01:01,362 --> 00:01:03,035
<i>I don't have time.</i>

2
00:01:04,165 --> 00:01:07,009
<i>I don't have time to
worry about haw it happened.</i>

3
00:01:07,535 --> 00:01:09,310
<i>It is what it is.</i>

4
00:01:10,171 --> 00:01:14,017
<i>We're genetically engineered
to stop aging at 25.</i>

5
00:01:14,842 --> 00:01:18,085
<i>The trouble is,
we live only one more year</i>

6
00:01:18,846 --> 00:01:21,019
<i>unless we can get more time.</i>

7
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:26,855
<i>Time is now the currency.</i>

8
00:01:27,922 --> 00:01:30,528
<i>We earn it and spend it.</i>

9
00:01:31,526 --> 00:01:33,870
<i>The rich can live forever.</i>

10
00:01:34,696 --> 00:01:36,107
<i>And the rest of us?</i>

11
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:39,839
<i>I just want to wake up
with more time on my hand</i>

12
00:01:39,901 --> 00:01:41,608
<i>than hours in the day.</i>

13
00:02:13,134 --> 00:02:14,204
Hey, Mom.

14
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:16,174
You got in late last night.

15
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:17,841
I put in some overtime.

16
00:02:18,005 --> 00:02:19,143
Where'd it go?

17
00:02:19,674 --> 00:02:20,675
On you.

18
00:02:21,008 --> 00:02:23,716
They drink it in New Greenwich.
Happy 50th!

19
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:25,880
Fifty?

20
00:02:26,347 --> 00:02:27,690
That's right.

21
00:02:28,416 --> 00:02:30,589
Twenty-five for the 25th time.

22
00:02:30,852 --> 00:02:33,594
Oh, I was sure I'd have
a grandchild by now.

23
00:02:33,855 --> 00:02:34,856
Here we go.

24
00:02:34,922 --> 00:02:36,642
Bela's daughter is always asking about you.

25
00:02:36,691 --> 00:02:40,366
Who has time for a girlfriend?
Besides, what's the hurry?

26
00:02:40,928 --> 00:02:42,271
What do you got?

27
00:02:42,864 --> 00:02:44,935
Three days. Not even.

28
00:02:45,266 --> 00:02:46,609
We owe half that in rent.

29
00:02:46,667 --> 00:02:49,773
Eight for the electric and
we're still late on that loan.

30
00:02:49,871 --> 00:02:52,613
I can make extra on the side, you know.

31
00:02:53,541 --> 00:02:55,714
- I could...
- What, start fighting?

32
00:02:57,378 --> 00:02:58,379
Nobody wins.

33
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,081
Yeah.

34
00:03:01,349 --> 00:03:02,589
Remember, I'm not here tonight.

35
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:04,361
I got two days' work in
the garment district.

36
00:03:04,385 --> 00:03:05,863
- I know.
- Meet me at the bus stop tomorrow.

37
00:03:05,887 --> 00:03:08,367
- After I pay off the loan, I won't have long.
- I'll be there.

38
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:10,564
Will...

39
00:03:11,292 --> 00:03:14,296
I just wouldn't know what
to do if I lost you.

40
00:03:14,395 --> 00:03:15,567
I'm late.

41
00:03:15,797 --> 00:03:18,403
Let me give you 30 minutes
so you can have a decent lunch.

42
00:03:33,314 --> 00:03:34,418
I love you.

43
00:03:35,817 --> 00:03:37,421
Happy birthday, Mom.

44
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,560
When you get back,
we're going to celebrate.

45
00:03:50,932 --> 00:03:52,104
Will!

46
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:53,434
Will!

47
00:03:54,435 --> 00:03:55,436
You got a minute?

48
00:03:55,603 --> 00:03:57,763
What are you talking about, Mya?
You have a whole year.

49
00:03:58,306 --> 00:03:59,683
Not a year I can use yet.

50
00:04:00,274 --> 00:04:02,515
Come on, Will. I've got bills to pay.

51
00:04:05,613 --> 00:04:07,820
Here, take five minutes.

52
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,692
Get out of here.

53
00:04:28,469 --> 00:04:30,540
Four minutes for a cup of coffee?

54
00:04:30,605 --> 00:04:32,050
Yesterday, it was three.

55
00:04:32,139 --> 00:04:34,050
You want coffee or you want to reminisce?

56
00:04:34,308 --> 00:04:35,651
Two coffees.

57
00:04:38,713 --> 00:04:40,873
- How many shifts you got today, Borel?
- Just the two.

58
00:04:41,649 --> 00:04:43,492
Really excited about it.

59
00:04:45,486 --> 00:04:48,729
If you had any of your father in you,
we could make a fortune.

60
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:50,835
I don't fight.

61
00:04:55,496 --> 00:04:57,908
There's another one. Broad daylight.

62
00:05:31,198 --> 00:05:33,838
Whoa, what is this? Where's the rest?

63
00:05:34,035 --> 00:05:35,070
Never met the quota.

64
00:05:35,136 --> 00:05:36,615
My units are up from last week.

65
00:05:36,771 --> 00:05:38,546
So's the quota. Next.

66
00:05:38,606 --> 00:05:39,744
That's a joke, right?

67
00:05:40,107 --> 00:05:42,246
- Next.
- Move it. You're taking forever.

68
00:06:00,628 --> 00:06:01,902
You in, Will?

69
00:06:01,963 --> 00:06:03,738
I don't have time to gamble any more.

70
00:06:03,965 --> 00:06:05,467
Oh, thank God.

71
00:06:05,566 --> 00:06:08,570
Because ever since you stopped playing,
I started winning.

72
00:06:08,636 --> 00:06:09,808
You still owe me an hour.

73
00:06:12,573 --> 00:06:13,916
You seen Borel?

74
00:06:21,749 --> 00:06:23,592
- Will!
- Hey, man.

75
00:06:24,318 --> 00:06:25,362
Your wife's looking for you.

76
00:06:25,386 --> 00:06:26,463
You're not gonna believe it.

77
00:06:26,487 --> 00:06:30,299
This madman's been buying drinks all night.
He's got a century!

78
00:06:31,993 --> 00:06:33,666
Come on, let me get you home.

79
00:06:33,995 --> 00:06:35,941
Soon as I finish this drink.

80
00:06:36,597 --> 00:06:38,270
Hey! You!

81
00:06:38,733 --> 00:06:39,734
You!

82
00:06:40,835 --> 00:06:42,178
More everything!

83
00:06:45,106 --> 00:06:47,177
Do you want to come home with me?

84
00:06:47,274 --> 00:06:49,618
You can take us both home.

85
00:06:58,119 --> 00:06:59,359
Excuse me.

86
00:07:00,354 --> 00:07:02,129
You need to get out of here.

87
00:07:02,456 --> 00:07:03,958
Somebody's gonna clean that clock.

88
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:05,195
Yes!

89
00:07:07,962 --> 00:07:10,943
I mean, they aren't going to rob you.
They are going to kill you.

90
00:07:11,866 --> 00:07:12,909
They can't take that much time

91
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,378
and let you live to tell about it.

92
00:07:14,468 --> 00:07:15,469
Yes.

93
00:07:15,703 --> 00:07:18,877
I don't think you understand.
You should not be here!

94
00:07:26,113 --> 00:07:27,717
Will. Will!

95
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:30,493
Minutemen!

96
00:07:30,718 --> 00:07:32,288
Minutemen! Walk away, Will.

97
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,030
Those gangsters aren't playing around.

98
00:07:38,025 --> 00:07:39,368
Wait, wait.

99
00:07:39,827 --> 00:07:43,172
He's asking for it. Let's go.
He's not one of us.

100
00:07:43,898 --> 00:07:45,241
You think he'd help us?

101
00:07:46,233 --> 00:07:48,736
Don't worry. I won't do anything stupid.

102
00:07:49,336 --> 00:07:50,337
Go.

103
00:07:55,976 --> 00:07:57,546
The name's Fortis.

104
00:08:00,014 --> 00:08:03,518
And that, sir, is a very nice watch.

105
00:08:07,188 --> 00:08:10,692
Do you mind if I try it on?
I think it would suit me.

106
00:08:13,194 --> 00:08:14,605
I'll tell you what.

107
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:17,703
I'll fight you for it.

108
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,270
Come on.

109
00:08:21,602 --> 00:08:24,708
I'm an old man. Turned 75 last week.

110
00:08:34,115 --> 00:08:35,287
I need a moment.

111
00:08:51,398 --> 00:08:52,809
You ready to go?

112
00:08:54,969 --> 00:08:56,141
Ready to go.

113
00:09:00,074 --> 00:09:01,417
Let's get you out of here.

114
00:09:04,578 --> 00:09:05,921
Get him!

115
00:09:06,747 --> 00:09:10,092
Stop. What are you doing?
I can take care of myself.

116
00:09:10,151 --> 00:09:11,755
Yeah, it looked like it.

117
00:09:13,921 --> 00:09:15,059
I know what I'm doing.

118
00:09:15,122 --> 00:09:16,328
Run. Run!

119
00:09:29,436 --> 00:09:30,676
Come on!

120
00:09:31,772 --> 00:09:33,183
Here!

121
00:09:35,943 --> 00:09:37,013
Hurry!

122
00:09:42,116 --> 00:09:43,356
Move!

123
00:09:53,627 --> 00:09:55,971
Where the hell are you going? Get in here!

124
00:10:38,639 --> 00:10:40,482
I know who took him.

125
00:10:40,908 --> 00:10:42,751
I know who he is.

126
00:10:45,346 --> 00:10:46,848
Who he was.

127
00:10:54,388 --> 00:10:56,595
Damn it, damn it.

128
00:11:00,094 --> 00:11:02,267
What the hell are you doing here?

129
00:11:02,529 --> 00:11:04,202
Flashing all that?

130
00:11:04,398 --> 00:11:05,502
You out of your mind?

131
00:11:07,034 --> 00:11:08,104
Henry Hamilton.

132
00:11:11,538 --> 00:11:12,539
Will Salas.

133
00:11:21,282 --> 00:11:22,886
Ugh.

134
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:24,184
God.

135
00:11:24,451 --> 00:11:26,124
Drink more, it gets better.

136
00:11:33,294 --> 00:11:34,534
Not much better.

137
00:11:40,401 --> 00:11:41,903
You'll be safe till morning.

138
00:11:42,236 --> 00:11:43,909
I'll get you out of here.

139
00:11:45,406 --> 00:11:46,817
You're from New Greenwich.

140
00:11:48,309 --> 00:11:49,754
Does it show?

141
00:11:50,744 --> 00:11:51,916
Nah.

142
00:11:58,752 --> 00:12:00,925
Looks like you could use
some help yourself.

143
00:12:01,155 --> 00:12:02,498
No, thanks.

144
00:12:02,756 --> 00:12:04,326
How old are you?

145
00:12:05,159 --> 00:12:06,331
In real time?

146
00:12:07,094 --> 00:12:08,437
Twenty-eight.

147
00:12:08,929 --> 00:12:10,499
I'm 105.

148
00:12:10,764 --> 00:12:12,107
Good for you.

149
00:12:13,434 --> 00:12:16,608
You won't see 106, you have too many
more nights like tonight.

150
00:12:17,438 --> 00:12:18,781
You are right.

151
00:12:20,774 --> 00:12:22,776
But the day comes when you've had enough.

152
00:12:24,445 --> 00:12:27,449
Your mind can be spent,
even if your body's not.

153
00:12:30,284 --> 00:12:31,957
We want to die.

154
00:12:33,187 --> 00:12:34,427
We need to.

155
00:12:38,292 --> 00:12:42,138
That's your problem?
You've been alive too long?

156
00:12:45,532 --> 00:12:47,034
You ever known anyone who's died?

157
00:12:53,874 --> 00:12:56,548
For a few to be immortal, many must die.

158
00:13:02,149 --> 00:13:04,060
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

159
00:13:06,387 --> 00:13:08,389
You really don't know, do you?

160
00:13:10,824 --> 00:13:13,566
Everyone can't live forever.
Where would we put them?

161
00:13:16,997 --> 00:13:19,170
Why do you think there are Time Zones?

162
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:22,706
Why do you think taxes and prices go up

163
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:24,408
the same day in the ghetto?

164
00:13:26,407 --> 00:13:29,354
The cost of living keeps rising to
make sure people keep dying.

165
00:13:31,178 --> 00:13:32,956
How else could there be
men with a million years

166
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,425
while most live day to day?

167
00:13:38,852 --> 00:13:40,593
But the truth is

168
00:13:41,922 --> 00:13:43,265
there's more than enough.

169
00:13:46,026 --> 00:13:48,700
No one has to die before their time.

170
00:13:56,270 --> 00:14:00,616
If you had as much time
as I have on that clock,

171
00:14:03,076 --> 00:14:04,680
what would you do with it?

172
00:14:08,549 --> 00:14:10,222
I'd stop watching it.

173
00:14:14,455 --> 00:14:16,230
I can tell you one thing.

174
00:14:16,723 --> 00:14:18,725
If I had all that time,

175
00:14:19,393 --> 00:14:21,805
I sure as hell wouldn't waste it.

176
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:31,481
Get some rest.

177
00:14:35,476 --> 00:14:37,478
Don't worry. I won't take it in the night.

178
00:14:38,078 --> 00:14:39,989
And I won't take yours.

179
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:55,464
It does get better.

180
00:16:59,319 --> 00:17:01,094
- Oh, hey, Will.
- Hey, Greta.

181
00:17:01,989 --> 00:17:03,161
Is Borel in?

182
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:05,996
Yeah. Borel?

183
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,732
Look at that.

184
00:17:08,061 --> 00:17:10,598
A shame we gotta wait 25 years.

185
00:17:10,664 --> 00:17:12,007
We could use that year right now.

186
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:14,167
Borel?

187
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:18,344
I'm here.

188
00:17:21,008 --> 00:17:22,749
You'd better get her inside, Greta.

189
00:17:31,351 --> 00:17:32,694
Look at this.

190
00:17:35,255 --> 00:17:36,598
Where did you get that?

191
00:17:37,858 --> 00:17:39,428
The guy at the bar.

192
00:17:40,027 --> 00:17:41,768
They were going to kill him.

193
00:17:42,529 --> 00:17:44,202
He gave it to me.

194
00:17:45,766 --> 00:17:47,768
He timed himself out
before I could stop him.

195
00:17:47,868 --> 00:17:50,280
No one gives anybody 100 years.

196
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,914
He didn't just give me this.

197
00:17:52,973 --> 00:17:54,173
He gave me the truth about it.

198
00:17:54,207 --> 00:17:55,914
You can't let anyone see that.

199
00:17:56,543 --> 00:17:57,544
Hey.

200
00:17:57,711 --> 00:17:59,850
You know that time will get you killed.

201
00:18:06,053 --> 00:18:07,293
How long have we been friends?

202
00:18:08,522 --> 00:18:10,195
What, 10 years?

203
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:11,861
Here.

204
00:18:18,365 --> 00:18:19,708
A decade.

205
00:18:22,369 --> 00:18:23,677
You've been like a brother.

206
00:18:25,972 --> 00:18:27,144
Where are you going?

207
00:18:28,108 --> 00:18:30,110
Where this won't look out of place.

208
00:18:31,712 --> 00:18:34,249
I finally got the time to take my mom
to New Greenwich.

209
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:54,407
Greta, I'm going out!

210
00:18:55,235 --> 00:18:57,875
<i>Loan payment received,
two days. Thank you.</i>

211
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:07,647
Dayton.

212
00:19:08,148 --> 00:19:09,218
Two hours.

213
00:19:12,953 --> 00:19:14,159
It's always been an hour.

214
00:19:14,821 --> 00:19:16,596
Now it's two. Price went up.

215
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:17,657
Since when?

216
00:19:18,158 --> 00:19:19,330
Since today.

217
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,662
My son is meeting me.
He'll pay the difference.

218
00:19:22,763 --> 00:19:24,640
I can't do that, policy.

219
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:27,639
Please?

220
00:19:29,002 --> 00:19:30,845
It's a two-hour walk.

221
00:19:34,441 --> 00:19:36,182
I have an hour and a half.

222
00:19:39,279 --> 00:19:40,622
Then you'd better run.

223
00:20:13,647 --> 00:20:16,821
Stop! Please stop!

224
00:20:48,849 --> 00:20:52,353
Wait! Please! Please, no!

225
00:20:53,353 --> 00:20:55,424
Wait! No! Please!

226
00:21:17,043 --> 00:21:18,215
Mom?

227
00:21:18,278 --> 00:21:19,279
Will!

228
00:21:23,884 --> 00:21:25,227
Will!

229
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:27,898
- Will!
- Mom!

230
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,969
No, no, no, no!

231
00:21:55,649 --> 00:21:56,753
No!

232
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:59,255
Mom, Mom, Mom!

233
00:22:25,412 --> 00:22:26,550
Thirteen zeros.

234
00:22:27,113 --> 00:22:28,615
Unlucky for all.

235
00:22:29,950 --> 00:22:31,759
The last time anyone saw him alive,

236
00:22:31,818 --> 00:22:34,025
there was over a century on that clock.

237
00:22:35,021 --> 00:22:37,023
Around here, they'd kill you for a week.

238
00:22:37,123 --> 00:22:38,932
What was he doing in this Time Zone?

239
00:22:41,127 --> 00:22:42,299
What I was thinking

240
00:22:43,697 --> 00:22:46,041
was he might have brought this on himself.

241
00:22:46,132 --> 00:22:48,703
Interesting. How long
you been keeping time, Jaeger?

242
00:22:48,969 --> 00:22:50,073
Five years.

243
00:22:50,837 --> 00:22:53,277
Let me know what you think
when you have been doing it for 50.

244
00:22:54,107 --> 00:22:55,586
It doesn't matter why he came here.

245
00:22:55,642 --> 00:22:59,112
What matters are the hundred years
that came with him.

246
00:23:01,848 --> 00:23:03,521
Gotta be a witness.

247
00:23:03,850 --> 00:23:05,625
Trust me, no one saw anything.

248
00:23:05,685 --> 00:23:07,045
What would you like us to do, sir?

249
00:23:08,521 --> 00:23:11,365
What we always do. Follow the time.

250
00:23:15,128 --> 00:23:18,302
Hey, Ray. I'll give you 10 minutes
for an hour.

251
00:23:18,365 --> 00:23:20,076
When are you gonna
get out of the game, Leila?

252
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:21,306
You gotta be pushing 60.

253
00:23:21,468 --> 00:23:23,311
Thanks for letting everyone know.

254
00:23:34,748 --> 00:23:35,783
<i>Am I in the right place?</i>

255
00:23:59,672 --> 00:24:02,846
We don't normally make
pickups in this Zone.

256
00:24:04,177 --> 00:24:05,850
I was lost.

257
00:24:12,085 --> 00:24:13,758
<i>Please deposit one month.</i>

258
00:24:38,711 --> 00:24:41,385
<i>Please deposit two months.</i>

259
00:24:49,722 --> 00:24:51,724
There are more of these than I remember.

260
00:25:03,536 --> 00:25:05,038
That was a year.

261
00:25:05,572 --> 00:25:07,415
Welcome to New Greenwich.

262
00:25:10,076 --> 00:25:11,919
What are you really doing here?

263
00:25:13,913 --> 00:25:16,416
I'm going to take them
for everything they've got.

264
00:25:20,987 --> 00:25:22,762
I'm going to make them pay.

265
00:26:25,818 --> 00:26:27,991
Please, miss. You can't be too careful.

266
00:26:28,054 --> 00:26:29,761
Are you sure?

267
00:26:32,825 --> 00:26:34,099
What's a night here cost?

268
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:36,140
Two months for a standard room.

269
00:26:39,899 --> 00:26:41,003
Give me a suite.

270
00:26:52,512 --> 00:26:53,792
Do you need help with your bags?

271
00:26:54,581 --> 00:26:55,753
No.

272
00:27:07,193 --> 00:27:09,696
- He's fast.
- He's going to have to be.

273
00:27:10,363 --> 00:27:13,207
The camera doesn't show us
how the body got into the river.

274
00:27:13,266 --> 00:27:15,041
What do we really know?

275
00:27:15,134 --> 00:27:17,205
What do we know?

276
00:27:17,270 --> 00:27:20,717
We know that most thefts in Dayton
amount to hours or days.

277
00:27:21,274 --> 00:27:23,049
This was a century.

278
00:27:24,377 --> 00:27:26,448
I don't see any more in circulation.

279
00:27:27,413 --> 00:27:28,756
He could have capsuled the time.

280
00:27:29,048 --> 00:27:31,460
You can't hide a hundred years
in the ghetto.

281
00:27:31,718 --> 00:27:34,722
They can sense when a man has
a month more than he should.

282
00:27:37,457 --> 00:27:39,061
The time left town.

283
00:28:24,437 --> 00:28:26,678
That'll be eight and a half weeks.

284
00:28:28,941 --> 00:28:30,443
Take a week for yourself.

285
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:32,282
Thanks.

286
00:28:37,517 --> 00:28:41,192
You're not from around here, are you?

287
00:28:43,022 --> 00:28:45,298
You do everything a little too fast.

288
00:28:46,459 --> 00:28:47,494
Not everything.

289
00:28:49,462 --> 00:28:50,902
What's that place across the street?

290
00:28:51,864 --> 00:28:53,036
The casino.

291
00:28:53,299 --> 00:28:54,972
Can anybody go?

292
00:28:56,536 --> 00:28:57,640
Not dressed like that.

293
00:28:58,971 --> 00:29:00,314
Good luck.

294
00:29:06,979 --> 00:29:09,050
Sir, you were right.

295
00:29:09,148 --> 00:29:11,685
If you turn back the clocks
the day of Hamilton's death,

296
00:29:11,751 --> 00:29:12,889
and look at the time checks,

297
00:29:12,952 --> 00:29:15,933
someone spent years crossing
four different Time Zones from Dayton...

298
00:29:15,988 --> 00:29:20,334
To New Greenwich. The cameras picked up
on his suspicious behavior.

299
00:29:20,393 --> 00:29:22,566
He's conscious of the surveillance,

300
00:29:22,628 --> 00:29:25,404
he doesn't have a bodyguard, and he runs.

301
00:29:25,665 --> 00:29:28,009
But if he has time, he doesn't need to run.

302
00:29:28,234 --> 00:29:30,180
It's a hard habit to break.

303
00:29:31,904 --> 00:29:33,577
You're looking for a match?

304
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:36,345
His name is Will Salas.

305
00:29:36,909 --> 00:29:38,252
You know him?

306
00:29:39,178 --> 00:29:40,350
No.

307
00:29:41,848 --> 00:29:43,259
I remember his father.

308
00:29:51,023 --> 00:29:52,366
Good evening.

309
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,437
I assume my time is as good as anyone's.

310
00:29:56,529 --> 00:30:01,103
Indeed it is. However,
there is a voluntary donation

311
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:03,874
for non-members. Most give a year.

312
00:30:11,711 --> 00:30:13,054
What's your game?

313
00:30:13,379 --> 00:30:14,414
Poker.

314
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,720
Right this way.

315
00:30:18,117 --> 00:30:19,619
What's the limit?

316
00:30:20,386 --> 00:30:21,729
There is none.

317
00:30:35,802 --> 00:30:38,646
I don't believe we've had the pleasure
of your company before, Mr...

318
00:30:38,704 --> 00:30:40,149
Salas.

319
00:30:40,306 --> 00:30:41,410
Will Salas.

320
00:30:42,074 --> 00:30:45,817
Philippe Weis. You must come from time.

321
00:30:48,981 --> 00:30:51,052
You could say I'm gambling my inheritance.

322
00:30:51,117 --> 00:30:53,620
You don't have a guard, Mr. Salas?

323
00:30:56,823 --> 00:30:58,996
I assumed I was amongst friends.

324
00:31:05,998 --> 00:31:07,170
Bet you 50 years.

325
00:31:15,608 --> 00:31:17,110
You must be young.

326
00:31:17,944 --> 00:31:21,016
When you've been 25 for 85 years,
like I have,

327
00:31:21,113 --> 00:31:24,356
knowing only a random act of violence
can take your life,

328
00:31:24,851 --> 00:31:26,694
you learn to appreciate what you have.

329
00:31:27,787 --> 00:31:29,630
And you seem to have a lot to appreciate.

330
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:34,365
I call.

331
00:31:50,810 --> 00:31:54,986
Of course,
some think what we have is unfair.

332
00:31:55,715 --> 00:31:57,319
The time difference between Zones.

333
00:31:57,650 --> 00:31:58,993
I've heard that.

334
00:32:00,152 --> 00:32:02,655
But isn't this just the next logical step
in our evolution?

335
00:32:02,788 --> 00:32:05,667
And hasn't evolution always been unfair?

336
00:32:05,725 --> 00:32:07,365
It's always been survival of the fittest.

337
00:32:09,729 --> 00:32:12,005
Raise you another two centuries.

338
00:32:14,901 --> 00:32:17,905
This is merely Darwinian capitalism.

339
00:32:19,739 --> 00:32:20,911
Natural selection.

340
00:32:21,674 --> 00:32:23,017
Absolutely.

341
00:32:23,743 --> 00:32:25,416
The strong survive.

342
00:32:26,512 --> 00:32:28,514
And I think your hand is weak.

343
00:32:29,849 --> 00:32:31,192
I call.

344
00:32:46,432 --> 00:32:48,776
It appears you're all in, Mr. Salas.

345
00:33:19,465 --> 00:33:21,035
Thirteen figures.

346
00:33:22,468 --> 00:33:23,811
Well played.

347
00:33:25,404 --> 00:33:27,247
That was some risk.

348
00:33:31,777 --> 00:33:33,120
It wasn't a risk.

349
00:33:33,412 --> 00:33:36,757
No offense. I knew I was going to win.

350
00:33:38,918 --> 00:33:40,329
Confusing times.

351
00:33:42,088 --> 00:33:44,432
Is she my mother, my sister
or my daughter?

352
00:33:44,557 --> 00:33:46,468
You're hoping she's not my wife.

353
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:51,105
Things used to be simpler once.
So I'm told.

354
00:33:52,932 --> 00:33:54,104
Very beautiful.

355
00:33:55,835 --> 00:33:56,836
Daughter.

356
00:33:57,269 --> 00:34:00,944
Though she does look
a lot like my wife. Sylvia?

357
00:34:01,841 --> 00:34:03,252
Will Salas.

358
00:34:03,309 --> 00:34:04,788
Congratulations, Mr. Salas.

359
00:34:06,512 --> 00:34:08,514
You've taken years off my father's life.

360
00:34:08,614 --> 00:34:12,027
Which is normally what you do.
Isn't that right, my darling?

361
00:34:13,619 --> 00:34:15,621
We're having a party tomorrow night.

362
00:34:16,188 --> 00:34:19,533
Perhaps you'll give him a chance to
win back some of those years.

363
00:34:20,826 --> 00:34:21,964
I'd love to.

364
00:34:22,028 --> 00:34:23,735
Carl will tell you where I am.

365
00:34:23,796 --> 00:34:25,139
Good night, Mr. Salas.

366
00:34:25,631 --> 00:34:27,804
Sylvia, stay with your guards.

367
00:34:42,481 --> 00:34:44,324
Fifty-nine years.

368
00:34:44,550 --> 00:34:45,688
Plus tax.

369
00:34:57,563 --> 00:34:58,735
The price includes delivery.

370
00:34:59,665 --> 00:35:00,735
Delivery?

371
00:35:01,333 --> 00:35:03,335
To wherever you're going to display it.

372
00:35:05,004 --> 00:35:06,176
Display it?

373
00:35:06,405 --> 00:35:08,248
Hell, I'm going to drive it.

374
00:35:28,227 --> 00:35:29,228
Will Salas.

375
00:35:31,197 --> 00:35:33,541
Allow me to introduce
my mother-in-law, Clara,

376
00:35:34,266 --> 00:35:37,543
my wife, Michele, and my daughter, Sylvia.

377
00:35:37,703 --> 00:35:39,444
I believe you two have already met.

378
00:35:41,707 --> 00:35:43,209
Nice to meet you all.

379
00:35:43,342 --> 00:35:44,844
I'll come find you later

380
00:35:45,411 --> 00:35:46,617
for our game.

381
00:35:47,279 --> 00:35:48,883
I look forward to it.

382
00:36:04,130 --> 00:36:06,132
Having fun, Mr. Salas?

383
00:36:08,734 --> 00:36:10,077
Please, call me Will.

384
00:36:11,237 --> 00:36:13,080
It's okay, Constantin.

385
00:36:15,908 --> 00:36:18,912
Do you always have a hired hand
standing right next to you?

386
00:36:18,978 --> 00:36:20,480
No. I usually have two.

387
00:36:23,082 --> 00:36:25,153
That doesn't make it very easy
to get to know you.

388
00:36:25,317 --> 00:36:26,990
I think that's the idea.

389
00:36:27,253 --> 00:36:28,755
Your idea?

390
00:36:28,821 --> 00:36:29,891
My father's.

391
00:36:29,955 --> 00:36:31,093
I understand.

392
00:36:32,091 --> 00:36:34,093
You all have a lot to lose.

393
00:36:34,927 --> 00:36:36,429
So do you.

394
00:36:39,431 --> 00:36:41,104
What do you do, Will?

395
00:36:41,767 --> 00:36:43,769
I haven't quite figured that out yet.

396
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:48,274
Yes, why bother? What's the hurry?

397
00:36:49,341 --> 00:36:52,686
Right. Why do today what
you can do in a century?

398
00:36:53,679 --> 00:36:55,022
I know one thing we can do.

399
00:36:58,050 --> 00:36:59,688
Dance with me.

400
00:37:06,225 --> 00:37:08,296
Do you really come from time?

401
00:37:09,395 --> 00:37:11,068
Why would you doubt that?

402
00:37:13,632 --> 00:37:15,236
I saw you run.

403
00:37:16,235 --> 00:37:18,738
Reminds me of people
who come from the ghetto.

404
00:37:21,907 --> 00:37:23,909
Sometimes I envy them.

405
00:37:27,079 --> 00:37:28,752
You don't know anything.

406
00:37:30,082 --> 00:37:33,586
Oh, no? The clock is good for no one.

407
00:37:36,255 --> 00:37:38,599
The poor die and the rich don't live.

408
00:37:38,991 --> 00:37:42,336
We can all live forever as long as
we don't do anything foolish.

409
00:37:43,095 --> 00:37:47,771
Doesn't that scare you? That maybe
you'll never do anything foolish?

410
00:37:48,100 --> 00:37:51,775
Or courageous or anything worth a damn?

411
00:37:57,610 --> 00:37:58,782
Come with me.

412
00:38:13,859 --> 00:38:15,532
This was tonight.

413
00:38:18,197 --> 00:38:20,302
He's only an hour ahead of us.

414
00:38:27,473 --> 00:38:28,975
Look at that.

415
00:38:30,142 --> 00:38:31,985
I've never seen anything like it.

416
00:38:35,447 --> 00:38:36,790
What are you doing?

417
00:38:38,651 --> 00:38:39,891
We don't go in.

418
00:38:42,655 --> 00:38:44,225
You're insane.

419
00:38:44,657 --> 00:38:47,831
You have this in your backyard.
You never go in.

420
00:38:49,328 --> 00:38:50,671
And I'm insane?

421
00:38:55,668 --> 00:38:58,672
Well? What are you waiting for?

422
00:39:00,406 --> 00:39:02,079
Sylvia, come on!

423
00:39:02,841 --> 00:39:05,344
What happened to doing something foolish?

424
00:39:27,099 --> 00:39:28,942
I don't know you.

425
00:39:30,869 --> 00:39:32,439
We could change that.

426
00:39:35,374 --> 00:39:36,717
I get it.

427
00:39:37,843 --> 00:39:40,687
You're out here, all alone,

428
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:42,886
with a stranger.

429
00:39:44,316 --> 00:39:45,989
You can't be too careful.

430
00:39:47,286 --> 00:39:48,390
Maybe you can.

431
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:51,060
Sylvia!

432
00:39:53,392 --> 00:39:54,564
Sylvia!

433
00:40:04,737 --> 00:40:06,580
I have to go back.

434
00:40:07,639 --> 00:40:08,982
To what?

435
00:40:15,147 --> 00:40:16,820
You should go back.

436
00:40:28,761 --> 00:40:31,173
- Have you seen my daughter?
- I have.

437
00:40:32,631 --> 00:40:33,632
She's with her guards.

438
00:40:35,601 --> 00:40:36,944
Right behind you.

439
00:40:39,772 --> 00:40:41,115
Thank God.

440
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:43,012
Now,

441
00:40:43,509 --> 00:40:44,613
how about that game?

442
00:40:53,685 --> 00:40:56,359
It's all right, everyone.
What's this about?

443
00:40:58,791 --> 00:41:00,862
I'm sorry to have to
break up the party, Mr. Weis.

444
00:41:02,294 --> 00:41:03,734
I just need a word with your friend.

445
00:41:06,131 --> 00:41:07,474
My friend?

446
00:41:08,700 --> 00:41:10,043
Very well.

447
00:41:37,396 --> 00:41:39,342
I'm Timekeeper Raymond Leon.

448
00:41:43,435 --> 00:41:44,436
I'm Will Salas.

449
00:41:44,503 --> 00:41:45,846
I know.

450
00:41:49,408 --> 00:41:50,751
What are you doing in this Zone?

451
00:41:51,844 --> 00:41:54,347
It's not illegal, is it?
To change Time Zones?

452
00:41:55,013 --> 00:41:56,856
No, it's not illegal.

453
00:41:58,016 --> 00:42:00,189
It's just rare.

454
00:42:05,257 --> 00:42:06,361
Where did you get that?

455
00:42:06,592 --> 00:42:07,764
I won it.

456
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:10,103
Gambling.

457
00:42:13,532 --> 00:42:14,704
All of it?

458
00:42:20,205 --> 00:42:21,275
No.

459
00:42:22,374 --> 00:42:24,877
A man named Henry Hamilton
gave me over a century.

460
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:30,226
He said he didn't need it any more.

461
00:42:31,950 --> 00:42:33,554
He timed himself out.

462
00:42:34,286 --> 00:42:37,233
Henry Hamilton was
worth thousands of years.

463
00:42:37,890 --> 00:42:39,961
He could practically live forever.

464
00:42:41,560 --> 00:42:46,532
You expect me to believe that
he was immortal and he wanted to die?

465
00:42:47,232 --> 00:42:49,234
I don't expect you to believe it.

466
00:42:50,636 --> 00:42:51,808
But it's the truth.

467
00:42:53,939 --> 00:42:55,282
It was a gift.

468
00:42:56,074 --> 00:42:57,314
I'm not a thief.

469
00:42:59,411 --> 00:43:02,415
But, hey, if you guys
are looking for stolen time,

470
00:43:03,982 --> 00:43:05,586
maybe you should arrest everyone here.

471
00:43:05,817 --> 00:43:06,921
Oh, I see.

472
00:43:07,986 --> 00:43:09,431
You're talking about justice.

473
00:43:11,156 --> 00:43:13,329
Well, I am a Timekeeper.

474
00:43:13,759 --> 00:43:16,433
I don't concern myself with "justice."

475
00:43:16,929 --> 00:43:20,103
I only concern myself
with what I can measure.

476
00:43:20,599 --> 00:43:23,102
Seconds, minutes, hours.

477
00:43:25,604 --> 00:43:26,674
I keep time.

478
00:43:28,507 --> 00:43:31,010
And that time is in the wrong hands.

479
00:43:33,612 --> 00:43:36,957
That time will be held, along with you.

480
00:43:40,352 --> 00:43:42,855
We'll leave you two hours
for booking and processing.

481
00:43:46,525 --> 00:43:48,471
Why are you investigating a suicide?

482
00:43:50,963 --> 00:43:52,772
There's mass murder
in the ghetto every day.

483
00:43:59,871 --> 00:44:01,373
That is fascinating.

484
00:44:02,774 --> 00:44:03,775
Huh.

485
00:44:05,477 --> 00:44:07,718
I heard another man talk like that.

486
00:44:09,147 --> 00:44:11,149
It was over 20 years ago.

487
00:44:14,052 --> 00:44:16,726
You're probably too young
to remember your father.

488
00:44:18,323 --> 00:44:20,325
We'll arrange safe transport.

489
00:44:21,159 --> 00:44:23,230
This is New Greenwich, after all.

490
00:44:28,066 --> 00:44:30,706
Sylvia? Do as I say and go with the guards.

491
00:44:30,836 --> 00:44:33,510
Oh, for God's sake, Father.
There's an army in this house.

492
00:44:33,839 --> 00:44:37,912
If we can't stop one man from killing us,
we should kill ourselves.

493
00:44:59,998 --> 00:45:01,341
Stop him!

494
00:45:04,102 --> 00:45:06,878
Move! Get out of the way!

495
00:45:11,710 --> 00:45:13,781
Put it down or I'll blow her head off.

496
00:45:15,280 --> 00:45:16,554
Thanks.

497
00:45:55,754 --> 00:45:58,325
You're going to kill us!
Please just let me out!

498
00:46:24,082 --> 00:46:25,152
What are you doing?

499
00:46:27,586 --> 00:46:29,088
Do you even know how to drive?

500
00:46:29,855 --> 00:46:31,357
What's there to know?

501
00:46:45,704 --> 00:46:46,978
Oh, shit.

502
00:47:23,575 --> 00:47:25,020
Give me some time.

503
00:47:27,579 --> 00:47:29,539
I guess you really are
from the ghetto, after all.

504
00:47:30,081 --> 00:47:33,187
What the hell do you know about
where I'm from? Give me some time.

505
00:47:33,585 --> 00:47:35,929
Or you're gonna kill me,
like you killed Henry Hamilton?

506
00:47:36,388 --> 00:47:37,731
Lend me an hour.

507
00:47:38,256 --> 00:47:39,376
I'm not giving you a second.

508
00:47:41,927 --> 00:47:43,406
I should have listened to my father.

509
00:47:45,864 --> 00:47:48,367
Please, take me home. Please.

510
00:47:48,934 --> 00:47:50,379
- I can't do that.
- Why?

511
00:47:50,702 --> 00:47:52,045
You're keeping me alive.

512
00:47:54,272 --> 00:47:55,615
Keep that covered.

513
00:47:56,241 --> 00:47:58,585
Anybody sees it, you're definitely dead.

514
00:48:32,878 --> 00:48:34,721
Now that worked too well.

515
00:48:34,779 --> 00:48:37,055
You guys wasted a gorgeous car.

516
00:48:37,382 --> 00:48:38,884
Look who it is.

517
00:48:39,117 --> 00:48:40,562
Who it was.

518
00:48:43,788 --> 00:48:45,131
He's done in minutes.

519
00:48:45,390 --> 00:48:48,462
He'll wake up dead. That'll be a shock.

520
00:48:48,960 --> 00:48:52,305
Too bad. I would have preferred to
kill him more beautifully.

521
00:48:52,564 --> 00:48:54,134
The girl's still breathing.

522
00:48:54,900 --> 00:48:55,901
She's got a decade.

523
00:48:57,235 --> 00:48:58,578
Holy shit.

524
00:48:58,770 --> 00:49:01,444
The man he stole from me
had more than a century.

525
00:49:06,411 --> 00:49:08,652
What? We'll divide it later.

526
00:49:09,080 --> 00:49:10,923
It's like an angel fell from the sky.

527
00:49:15,921 --> 00:49:17,093
Fortis!

528
00:49:17,155 --> 00:49:18,361
Leave it!

529
00:49:18,657 --> 00:49:19,761
Fortis!

530
00:49:46,451 --> 00:49:47,794
Look at me.

531
00:49:48,019 --> 00:49:49,362
You okay?

532
00:49:49,788 --> 00:49:50,960
No.

533
00:49:53,458 --> 00:49:54,528
Why are you laughing?

534
00:49:56,027 --> 00:49:57,062
We're not dead.

535
00:49:57,162 --> 00:49:58,722
Yeah, we're not alive for long, either.

536
00:49:59,364 --> 00:50:02,038
Where did my time go? I have a half hour!

537
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:03,570
Ah.

538
00:50:03,635 --> 00:50:05,046
You're lucky.

539
00:50:05,804 --> 00:50:08,216
- Minutemen.
- Does everyone in the ghetto steal?

540
00:50:08,306 --> 00:50:09,546
That's rich, coming from you.

541
00:50:10,709 --> 00:50:12,416
- Please help me, Will.
- Let me guess,

542
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:14,717
now you like the idea of sharing.

543
00:50:16,881 --> 00:50:18,053
Come here.

544
00:50:20,719 --> 00:50:23,325
Hey, don't worry. It's not the
first time I've been this broke.

545
00:50:23,555 --> 00:50:25,330
Well, it's a first for me.

546
00:50:26,725 --> 00:50:28,398
What are we going to do?

547
00:50:28,660 --> 00:50:31,664
Whatever we have to.
Come on, we got to go.

548
00:50:51,683 --> 00:50:54,061
Dispatch, wire me my per diem.

549
00:50:54,386 --> 00:50:56,229
<i>Time transfer.</i>

550
00:51:00,759 --> 00:51:02,705
Cutting it close again, sir.

551
00:51:03,028 --> 00:51:05,201
Well, I'm still walking around.

552
00:51:05,930 --> 00:51:07,375
Judging by the lack of dead bodies,

553
00:51:07,432 --> 00:51:09,878
I have to assume they are also.

554
00:51:14,539 --> 00:51:18,214
They got jacked. They couldn't have
left here with more than minutes.

555
00:51:18,443 --> 00:51:20,548
He's back in his old neighborhood.

556
00:51:21,946 --> 00:51:24,119
So, where do you want us to start looking?

557
00:51:25,717 --> 00:51:28,960
We don't. He'll come to us.

558
00:51:49,574 --> 00:51:50,848
Borel?

559
00:51:53,912 --> 00:51:55,914
Borel, open up. It's Will.

560
00:51:58,083 --> 00:51:59,255
Greta.

561
00:52:01,086 --> 00:52:02,292
Where's Borel?

562
00:52:03,254 --> 00:52:04,927
He's dead.

563
00:52:05,924 --> 00:52:08,268
Dead? What?

564
00:52:08,493 --> 00:52:09,699
You gave him a decade.

565
00:52:11,162 --> 00:52:13,802
He drank himself to death
with nine years on his clock.

566
00:52:13,865 --> 00:52:15,208
Jesus Christ.

567
00:52:18,203 --> 00:52:19,682
Greta, I'm so sorry.

568
00:52:20,872 --> 00:52:22,374
Goodbye, Will.

569
00:52:30,482 --> 00:52:31,517
Will, we have minutes.

570
00:52:31,583 --> 00:52:32,653
Try not to act like it.

571
00:52:32,717 --> 00:52:34,594
- What is that supposed to mean?
- Shut up!

572
00:52:34,686 --> 00:52:36,363
We're going to die, Will!
Do you want to die?

573
00:52:36,387 --> 00:52:37,730
Shut up!

574
00:52:43,561 --> 00:52:46,007
I hope those are real. Run.

575
00:52:57,842 --> 00:52:58,912
Stop! Wait!

576
00:52:59,010 --> 00:53:00,114
Please, wait!

577
00:53:02,247 --> 00:53:03,749
Come back in an hour.

578
00:53:03,848 --> 00:53:05,350
That won't be possible.

579
00:53:07,952 --> 00:53:09,124
Here!

580
00:53:23,935 --> 00:53:25,215
I'll give you two days for them.

581
00:53:25,537 --> 00:53:26,641
They're diamonds.

582
00:53:26,871 --> 00:53:29,112
You can take the 48 hours,
or you can be a pretty corpse.

583
00:53:29,707 --> 00:53:30,879
We'll take it.

584
00:53:41,886 --> 00:53:43,263
Don't make a sound.

585
00:53:43,321 --> 00:53:44,664
Give me my time.

586
00:53:51,496 --> 00:53:52,497
Let's go.

587
00:53:54,265 --> 00:53:56,108
I guess I got my wish.

588
00:53:56,167 --> 00:53:58,306
I did do something foolish.

589
00:54:01,105 --> 00:54:02,948
Your name's on a lot of buildings.

590
00:54:03,007 --> 00:54:04,611
It's my father's name.

591
00:54:04,776 --> 00:54:06,847
How much is he worth, anyway?

592
00:54:08,112 --> 00:54:09,455
Eons.

593
00:54:09,848 --> 00:54:11,794
What do you think he'd pay to get you back?

594
00:54:12,016 --> 00:54:14,292
You have no shame, do you?

595
00:54:18,289 --> 00:54:20,633
<i>Please deposit one minute.</i>

596
00:54:22,794 --> 00:54:23,864
Dial.

597
00:54:38,309 --> 00:54:39,310
Hello.

598
00:54:39,377 --> 00:54:42,324
Mr. Weis, please give the phone
to the Timekeeper.

599
00:54:48,152 --> 00:54:51,156
Hello, Will. How much do you want?

600
00:54:51,990 --> 00:54:53,060
A thousand years.

601
00:54:54,225 --> 00:54:55,568
You'll never live to spend it.

602
00:55:00,665 --> 00:55:02,838
Then distribute it
to the Time Lines in Dayton.

603
00:55:04,335 --> 00:55:06,679
Do it by sunrise tomorrow
and she can go home.

604
00:55:09,474 --> 00:55:10,646
Will...

605
00:55:12,176 --> 00:55:14,019
I'm afraid for you, Will.

606
00:55:14,345 --> 00:55:17,554
You keep talking like him,
you're going to die like him.

607
00:55:17,749 --> 00:55:21,253
My father died in a fight,
trying to take a man's time.

608
00:55:21,352 --> 00:55:24,526
Oh, no. His crime wasn't taking time.

609
00:55:25,757 --> 00:55:28,033
<i>He was doing something
far more dangerous.</i>

610
00:55:29,928 --> 00:55:31,771
Please don't make your father's mistake.

611
00:55:38,202 --> 00:55:39,943
Dayton. Padre Plaza.

612
00:55:40,271 --> 00:55:41,614
I know it.

613
00:55:42,874 --> 00:55:45,718
A thousand years to the Time Lines.

614
00:55:45,944 --> 00:55:47,389
A thousand years.

615
00:55:49,948 --> 00:55:51,450
It's nothing.

616
00:55:51,716 --> 00:55:53,559
It's for our daughter.

617
00:55:55,286 --> 00:55:57,129
No, it's for them.

618
00:55:57,668 --> 00:55:59,170
This is insane.

619
00:55:59,236 --> 00:56:01,443
They can take your time, just like that.

620
00:56:02,606 --> 00:56:04,279
Or you can take theirs.

621
00:56:04,608 --> 00:56:06,110
This is insane.

622
00:56:06,777 --> 00:56:09,121
Yeah, it's insane.

623
00:56:23,126 --> 00:56:25,128
We should be safe here until dawn.

624
00:56:26,530 --> 00:56:29,306
I pay by the day.
It'll take them a while to find me.

625
00:56:34,871 --> 00:56:36,179
This is your place?

626
00:56:39,976 --> 00:56:42,718
There's water. It's cold,
but it's something.

627
00:56:43,980 --> 00:56:46,153
You can put on fresh clothes.

628
00:57:17,347 --> 00:57:18,553
Where's your family?

629
00:57:20,584 --> 00:57:22,359
My mother timed out.

630
00:57:25,522 --> 00:57:26,592
This is her dress.

631
00:57:26,857 --> 00:57:28,029
Yeah.

632
00:57:31,595 --> 00:57:33,040
What about your father?

633
00:57:34,564 --> 00:57:35,907
He died when I was a boy.

634
00:57:37,033 --> 00:57:39,377
He was a fighter. Strong arm.

635
00:57:41,438 --> 00:57:45,215
He wasn't the strongest,
but he knew how to win.

636
00:57:46,877 --> 00:57:48,220
How do you win?

637
00:57:56,386 --> 00:57:57,729
I'll show you.

638
00:58:02,559 --> 00:58:05,904
What you do is let them
have the upper hand.

639
00:58:06,229 --> 00:58:09,733
Then, he'd let his time
go all the way down.

640
00:58:11,134 --> 00:58:12,579
Because he knew

641
00:58:13,236 --> 00:58:15,307
that when you were
down to your last seconds

642
00:58:16,072 --> 00:58:17,915
and they think it's over,

643
00:58:19,409 --> 00:58:21,753
they start watching your clock

644
00:58:25,482 --> 00:58:26,825
and forget to watch their own.

645
00:58:43,166 --> 00:58:44,839
He died in a fight?

646
00:58:48,104 --> 00:58:52,348
I think he was killed
for giving away what he won.

647
00:58:52,442 --> 00:58:54,615
He wasn't just giving them time.

648
00:58:55,445 --> 00:58:56,822
He was giving them hope.

649
00:59:02,118 --> 00:59:03,597
How long have you been this old?

650
00:59:04,287 --> 00:59:05,664
Twenty-five for three.

651
00:59:07,791 --> 00:59:09,464
Twenty-five for two.

652
00:59:12,162 --> 00:59:14,164
What was it like when your clock started?

653
00:59:17,968 --> 00:59:19,413
<i>I was in the street.</i>

654
00:59:19,469 --> 00:59:21,471
<i>It almost knocked me over.</i>

655
00:59:22,138 --> 00:59:24,709
<i>My year was gone in a week,
we were so in debt.</i>

656
00:59:25,141 --> 00:59:27,985
After that, I lived day to day.

657
00:59:29,880 --> 00:59:31,826
Mine was a little different.

658
00:59:33,650 --> 00:59:34,993
It woke me.

659
00:59:47,664 --> 00:59:49,337
<i>I looked in the mirror.</i>

660
00:59:50,834 --> 00:59:52,836
<i>I guess everybody does.</i>

661
00:59:54,905 --> 00:59:57,408
<i>That's what you're gonna look like
for the rest of your life.</i>

662
00:59:59,009 --> 01:00:01,080
My dad gave me a decade to celebrate.

663
01:00:03,346 --> 01:00:04,586
You must hate me.

664
01:00:06,683 --> 01:00:08,185
Where I come from.

665
01:00:09,019 --> 01:00:11,522
It's nobody's fault,
what they're born with.

666
01:00:32,943 --> 01:00:34,616
They open in a minute.

667
01:00:36,279 --> 01:00:38,452
Let's see how generous your father is now.

668
01:01:09,312 --> 01:01:11,152
The Timekeepers would
have never let him do it.

669
01:01:11,247 --> 01:01:12,817
You don't have to say that.

670
01:01:13,917 --> 01:01:16,761
How do you think my father
built all those buildings?

671
01:01:17,253 --> 01:01:19,597
By giving away a thousand years?

672
01:01:23,927 --> 01:01:25,270
Now what?

673
01:01:27,097 --> 01:01:28,508
You can go home.

674
01:01:30,600 --> 01:01:32,307
There's people on the streets.

675
01:01:32,369 --> 01:01:33,689
I can move without being spotted.

676
01:01:34,671 --> 01:01:35,775
What have you got?

677
01:01:38,675 --> 01:01:40,018
Eleven hours.

678
01:01:42,078 --> 01:01:43,955
How does anyone live like this?

679
01:01:44,014 --> 01:01:45,618
You don't generally sleep in.

680
01:01:53,690 --> 01:01:55,294
You can call for help.

681
01:01:55,959 --> 01:01:57,470
I'll watch from here,
I'll make sure you're safe.

682
01:01:57,494 --> 01:01:59,235
You know, you could fight this.

683
01:02:00,330 --> 01:02:02,250
I can say that running to
the ghetto was my idea.

684
01:02:03,533 --> 01:02:05,453
My father'd believe that,
he thinks I'm reckless.

685
01:02:06,836 --> 01:02:08,315
He has a lot of influence, Will.

686
01:02:08,371 --> 01:02:09,873
He can get you a lawyer.

687
01:02:09,973 --> 01:02:11,782
He can make a deal with those Timekeepers.

688
01:02:12,375 --> 01:02:14,375
I'm pretty sure
that Timekeeper doesn't make deals.

689
01:02:18,348 --> 01:02:20,191
What are you going to do?

690
01:02:20,350 --> 01:02:21,693
Steal?

691
01:02:23,853 --> 01:02:25,958
Is it stealing if it's already stolen?

692
01:02:28,958 --> 01:02:31,302
Here. Just in case.

693
01:02:32,862 --> 01:02:33,932
I'll be right here.

694
01:03:04,828 --> 01:03:07,172
<i>Please deposit one minute.</i>

695
01:03:12,335 --> 01:03:14,008
- Father?
- Sylvia?

696
01:03:14,237 --> 01:03:16,410
You couldn't spare a second, Father?

697
01:03:17,073 --> 01:03:18,416
I wish I could say I'm surprised.

698
01:03:24,347 --> 01:03:25,424
Did you hear what I just said?

699
01:03:25,448 --> 01:03:26,768
<i>You know I'd do anything for you.</i>

700
01:03:28,251 --> 01:03:29,355
They're coming to get you.

701
01:03:29,586 --> 01:03:31,259
<i>They know where you are.</i>

702
01:03:31,521 --> 01:03:32,659
Will, look out!

703
01:03:51,374 --> 01:03:53,513
Sorry to disappoint you,
we don't keep much on us.

704
01:03:54,711 --> 01:03:57,214
To discourage thieves like you.

705
01:04:02,619 --> 01:04:03,791
Think of this as a gift.

706
01:04:05,889 --> 01:04:07,061
Will! Come on!

707
01:04:29,479 --> 01:04:31,481
I didn't mean to shoot him.
I wanted to scare him.

708
01:04:31,581 --> 01:04:33,219
I think you did both.

709
01:04:33,917 --> 01:04:35,419
You could say thank you.

710
01:04:35,485 --> 01:04:37,829
Thank you. What have you got?

711
01:04:39,088 --> 01:04:40,499
Nine hours.

712
01:04:41,257 --> 01:04:44,261
Why did you give him time?
You should have taken it.

713
01:04:46,262 --> 01:04:48,606
Timekeepers live day to day.

714
01:04:50,166 --> 01:04:52,840
It'll be hours before the others show up.

715
01:04:53,102 --> 01:04:55,241
He could die in the ghetto.

716
01:04:55,305 --> 01:04:56,613
He still might.

717
01:04:57,106 --> 01:04:59,108
Timekeeper, what's the hurry?

718
01:04:59,342 --> 01:05:03,347
Stay a while.
You might like us if you got to know us!

719
01:05:07,183 --> 01:05:08,719
They're going to think you're with me.

720
01:05:08,785 --> 01:05:10,196
Yes.

721
01:05:12,355 --> 01:05:14,130
This is a mess.

722
01:05:14,524 --> 01:05:15,969
Welcome to my world.

723
01:05:19,963 --> 01:05:21,306
Back off!

724
01:05:23,132 --> 01:05:25,874
You've been shot.
I was worried you timed out.

725
01:05:27,370 --> 01:05:28,713
Where'd you get that?

726
01:05:41,351 --> 01:05:42,955
What are we going to do?

727
01:05:43,019 --> 01:05:45,090
We can't keep driving around in this car.

728
01:05:45,154 --> 01:05:46,360
It's a cop car.

729
01:05:47,890 --> 01:05:49,130
So let's make an arrest.

730
01:06:09,512 --> 01:06:10,923
Was I going too fast?

731
01:06:11,914 --> 01:06:13,689
Not fast enough.

732
01:06:14,083 --> 01:06:16,222
The mistake you made was stopping.

733
01:06:17,687 --> 01:06:20,691
Now, let's see who you got back there.

734
01:06:23,526 --> 01:06:25,836
Got to be a year or two nobody's using.

735
01:06:27,297 --> 01:06:28,298
Whoa!

736
01:06:30,600 --> 01:06:32,045
It went off.

737
01:06:32,368 --> 01:06:33,779
I was just trying to help.

738
01:06:40,877 --> 01:06:42,049
Come on.

739
01:06:44,213 --> 01:06:48,389
Now, I'd say, "Your money or your life,"
but since your money is your life...

740
01:06:49,052 --> 01:06:50,793
How dare you steal from me?

741
01:06:50,953 --> 01:06:52,455
- Don't think of it as stealing.
- No?

742
01:06:52,722 --> 01:06:54,724
Think of it as repossession.

743
01:06:54,791 --> 01:06:57,151
I'll leave you with
what I've had most every day of my life.

744
01:06:57,960 --> 01:06:59,462
- One day.
- One day?

745
01:07:00,630 --> 01:07:01,700
Are you insane?

746
01:07:02,598 --> 01:07:03,638
You can do a lot in a day.

747
01:07:06,903 --> 01:07:08,246
Those are pretty.

748
01:07:14,911 --> 01:07:16,049
I owe you these.

749
01:07:16,112 --> 01:07:17,750
You shouldn't have.

750
01:07:18,414 --> 01:07:19,757
You, out.

751
01:07:26,656 --> 01:07:29,500
<i>Will Salas, prime
suspect in the murder of Henry Hamilton,</i>

752
01:07:29,592 --> 01:07:32,539
<i>is believed to be traveling
with Sylvia Weis,</i>

753
01:07:32,595 --> 01:07:34,905
<i>daughter of finance magnate,
Philippe Weis.</i>

754
01:07:34,964 --> 01:07:37,240
Citizens are advised to exercise extreme...

755
01:07:40,837 --> 01:07:42,612
We look cute together.

756
01:07:46,609 --> 01:07:48,452
It doesn't say you're wanted.

757
01:07:50,113 --> 01:07:51,956
It doesn't say I'm not.

758
01:07:53,015 --> 01:07:55,359
You've forgotten I shot a cop.

759
01:07:56,619 --> 01:07:58,690
I admit, not very well.

760
01:07:59,455 --> 01:08:01,025
It was your first time.

761
01:08:03,793 --> 01:08:04,794
Hey.

762
01:08:05,128 --> 01:08:07,802
I can say I made you do all of it.

763
01:08:08,798 --> 01:08:10,471
You can go back.

764
01:08:10,700 --> 01:08:12,373
Go back to what?

765
01:08:14,036 --> 01:08:17,984
Do I really want to spend my whole life
trying not to die by mistake?

766
01:08:20,643 --> 01:08:23,385
A lot of people would say
being here is a mistake.

767
01:08:25,982 --> 01:08:27,655
I don't have a choice.

768
01:08:30,653 --> 01:08:32,690
I'm starting to think that I don't, either.

769
01:08:53,910 --> 01:08:57,414
I want to reassure you all
there is no cause for alarm.

770
01:08:57,480 --> 01:08:58,686
No ransom was paid.

771
01:08:59,015 --> 01:09:00,926
<i>Your Zone is at risk, Philippe.</i>

772
01:09:01,017 --> 01:09:03,691
<i>It puts us at risk. It can spreed.</i>

773
01:09:03,853 --> 01:09:06,697
<i>Too much time in the wrong hands
can crash the market.</i>

774
01:09:06,923 --> 01:09:09,096
This hostage situation
will be quickly resolved.

775
01:09:09,158 --> 01:09:10,637
Sir.

776
01:09:13,362 --> 01:09:16,775
Everything is under control.
We'll talk soon.

777
01:09:23,539 --> 01:09:25,678
Timekeeper. After this
regrettable incident,

778
01:09:25,741 --> 01:09:28,551
it's really not necessary
for you to come in person.

779
01:09:29,545 --> 01:09:33,220
I'm afraid it really is necessary.

780
01:09:36,452 --> 01:09:37,954
When can we hope for a rescue?

781
01:09:38,221 --> 01:09:40,030
I believe that's the point.

782
01:09:40,089 --> 01:09:41,966
She doesn't appear to want to be rescued.

783
01:09:43,726 --> 01:09:45,228
Mr. Leon.

784
01:09:46,729 --> 01:09:49,471
Raymond. May I call you Raymond?

785
01:09:51,734 --> 01:09:53,304
I blame myself.

786
01:09:54,303 --> 01:09:56,340
I invited the man into my home.

787
01:09:56,405 --> 01:09:58,407
He had so much time,
how was I supposed to know?

788
01:10:00,243 --> 01:10:04,589
Of course, Sylvia brought this on herself
by her lack of vigilance.

789
01:10:05,147 --> 01:10:07,650
That's why I always tried
to keep her close.

790
01:10:09,252 --> 01:10:12,597
But she is clearly under
Will Salas' control.

791
01:10:20,763 --> 01:10:22,640
If it's a matter of resources,

792
01:10:23,199 --> 01:10:25,645
I'm happy to make a contribution.

793
01:10:27,436 --> 01:10:29,677
It's a scandal,
what we pay our Timekeepers.

794
01:10:33,442 --> 01:10:35,615
I've issued a warrant
for your daughter's arrest.

795
01:10:36,279 --> 01:10:38,850
If she contacts you
and you assist her in any way,

796
01:10:38,948 --> 01:10:40,791
I will issue a warrant for your arrest.

797
01:10:52,128 --> 01:10:54,472
There is nothing I cannot buy.

798
01:10:56,799 --> 01:10:57,869
Now

799
01:10:59,702 --> 01:11:01,375
how many of my years do you want?

800
01:11:03,472 --> 01:11:05,474
There aren't enough years,

801
01:11:06,642 --> 01:11:10,784
even in your lifetime, Mr.
Weis. Good night.

802
01:11:15,985 --> 01:11:18,158
This is called a trigger.

803
01:11:18,854 --> 01:11:22,199
And you don't pull it until
you actually want to shoot something.

804
01:11:29,298 --> 01:11:30,572
I wanted to shoot something.

805
01:11:30,633 --> 01:11:31,668
Right.

806
01:11:36,205 --> 01:11:38,185
Will, if you get a lot of time,

807
01:11:40,476 --> 01:11:41,836
are you really gonna give it away?

808
01:11:42,878 --> 01:11:44,721
I've only ever had a day.

809
01:11:45,648 --> 01:11:47,218
How much do you need?

810
01:11:48,651 --> 01:11:50,362
How can you live with yourself
watching people die

811
01:11:50,386 --> 01:11:51,490
right next to you?

812
01:11:53,055 --> 01:11:54,659
You don't watch.

813
01:11:55,992 --> 01:11:57,494
You close your eyes.

814
01:12:07,169 --> 01:12:09,342
I can help you get all the time you want.

815
01:12:16,879 --> 01:12:19,485
I need to borrow a month.
What's the interest?

816
01:12:20,216 --> 01:12:21,991
Today's rate, 30 %.

817
01:12:23,219 --> 01:12:24,721
I can't pay it back.

818
01:12:24,987 --> 01:12:27,160
We can always come to some arrangement.

819
01:12:52,915 --> 01:12:54,087
Let's go.

820
01:12:56,686 --> 01:13:00,395
Ladies and gentlemen, I am happy to
announce that Weis Timelenders

821
01:13:00,456 --> 01:13:03,403
is now offering interest-free
loans with no payments.

822
01:13:03,459 --> 01:13:04,529
Ever.

823
01:13:04,593 --> 01:13:06,095
So help yourselves and take a day.

824
01:13:06,228 --> 01:13:07,764
Take a month. Hell, take a year.

825
01:13:07,930 --> 01:13:10,035
Come on. Help yourselves! Take it.

826
01:13:10,099 --> 01:13:11,578
Take the time. It's free.

827
01:13:46,969 --> 01:13:49,142
No one's watching their clocks, huh?

828
01:13:49,638 --> 01:13:52,016
Get out of here,
or I'll confiscate every second!

829
01:13:59,482 --> 01:14:01,189
Must've thought it was a drive-through.

830
01:14:34,116 --> 01:14:35,117
Turn around.

831
01:14:35,684 --> 01:14:36,719
Don't move.

832
01:14:36,786 --> 01:14:38,390
I don't have much.

833
01:14:38,454 --> 01:14:40,024
Everything I have, I give away.

834
01:14:40,122 --> 01:14:41,123
I know.

835
01:15:03,312 --> 01:15:05,314
Yes, sir, I do know that, sir.

836
01:15:06,816 --> 01:15:08,989
There are years that shouldn't be there.

837
01:15:13,322 --> 01:15:14,995
I will stop him, sir.

838
01:15:17,059 --> 01:15:18,231
Doesn't he understand

839
01:15:18,294 --> 01:15:20,740
he's hurting the very people
he's trying to help?

840
01:15:30,406 --> 01:15:31,749
Well, now.

841
01:15:32,708 --> 01:15:34,688
- Look at all that.
- Yeah.

842
01:15:35,344 --> 01:15:37,187
I finally had time to buy one of these.

843
01:15:39,849 --> 01:15:41,590
Let's not do anything I might regret.

844
01:16:15,217 --> 01:16:16,958
What was that about?

845
01:16:17,820 --> 01:16:19,265
I wasted 30 days.

846
01:16:19,321 --> 01:16:22,928
<i>Today, Sylvia Weis
withdrew some of her "inheritance"</i>

847
01:16:22,992 --> 01:16:25,472
<i>when she and Will Salas
robbed her father's time bank</i>

848
01:16:25,561 --> 01:16:28,132
<i>for the sixth time in a week.</i>

849
01:16:28,964 --> 01:16:29,965
I give her everything.

850
01:16:31,634 --> 01:16:33,238
Does she want to kill me?

851
01:16:33,802 --> 01:16:35,304
You were killing her, Philippe.

852
01:16:37,573 --> 01:16:39,246
You were suffocating her.

853
01:16:41,477 --> 01:16:43,150
You suffocate us all.

854
01:16:47,917 --> 01:16:48,987
Call.

855
01:16:55,257 --> 01:16:56,600
That's good.

856
01:16:57,159 --> 01:16:59,662
Just not as good as that.

857
01:16:59,728 --> 01:17:00,729
Ooh!

858
01:17:01,931 --> 01:17:03,933
You haven't forgotten how to play cards.

859
01:17:04,500 --> 01:17:06,844
Why did I play strip poker with you?

860
01:17:07,436 --> 01:17:08,938
Why did you?

861
01:17:15,144 --> 01:17:16,214
Sir.

862
01:17:16,779 --> 01:17:18,190
They're still there.

863
01:17:19,848 --> 01:17:21,452
How did you know, sir?

864
01:17:22,518 --> 01:17:24,862
This is where the hours and the days are.

865
01:17:26,855 --> 01:17:28,960
He's paid them all off.

866
01:17:29,858 --> 01:17:31,303
This is where I would hide.

867
01:17:39,201 --> 01:17:40,703
Put your clothes on.

868
01:17:47,676 --> 01:17:49,019
Stop!

869
01:17:50,813 --> 01:17:52,656
- We're trapped!
- No, we're not!

870
01:17:54,216 --> 01:17:55,718
Jump. They won't do it.

871
01:17:55,818 --> 01:17:56,888
We shouldn't do it.

872
01:18:03,659 --> 01:18:04,831
Come on!

873
01:18:13,836 --> 01:18:15,907
See? They won't jump.

874
01:18:18,907 --> 01:18:20,045
So much for your theory.

875
01:18:20,109 --> 01:18:21,349
Shit!

876
01:18:37,559 --> 01:18:38,731
Here!

877
01:18:39,194 --> 01:18:40,298
Go!

878
01:18:43,966 --> 01:18:46,139
Stop! Stop!

879
01:19:04,019 --> 01:19:05,597
I'm telling you, he'll
give up before we do!

880
01:19:05,621 --> 01:19:06,793
You sure about that?

881
01:19:08,290 --> 01:19:09,633
No.

882
01:19:28,143 --> 01:19:29,486
- Go.
- I can't.

883
01:19:29,578 --> 01:19:30,989
You can! Go!

884
01:19:33,582 --> 01:19:34,720
Un-fucking-believable!

885
01:19:49,331 --> 01:19:50,605
Hold on.

886
01:19:51,500 --> 01:19:52,877
You two look familiar.

887
01:19:56,171 --> 01:19:57,343
How about now?

888
01:20:23,532 --> 01:20:24,977
Welcome to the Century.

889
01:20:25,367 --> 01:20:28,314
Hi. We're looking for a
quiet place to stay.

890
01:20:29,071 --> 01:20:30,106
How many rooms?

891
01:20:30,739 --> 01:20:31,774
All of them.

892
01:20:32,574 --> 01:20:34,247
We were hoping for something long-term.

893
01:20:34,977 --> 01:20:37,821
Can we rely on the
discretion of your staff?

894
01:20:38,046 --> 01:20:40,048
I'm sure you can.

895
01:20:48,824 --> 01:20:50,667
I'm sorry. We're fully booked.

896
01:20:52,728 --> 01:20:54,071
Right.

897
01:21:03,572 --> 01:21:05,574
Nobody goes anywhere!

898
01:21:05,874 --> 01:21:06,875
Wait, whoa, whoa.

899
01:21:08,677 --> 01:21:09,678
Don't look at me.

900
01:21:11,413 --> 01:21:13,188
You know who I'm looking for.

901
01:21:17,352 --> 01:21:21,698
I'm looking for whoever
gave this man a month!

902
01:21:24,092 --> 01:21:28,097
And I'm gonna clean the clocks off
of every one of you in this hellhole

903
01:21:28,197 --> 01:21:32,737
until someone says something
I want to hear.

904
01:21:40,275 --> 01:21:41,618
I can't hear anything.

905
01:21:46,048 --> 01:21:47,220
Clean it.

906
01:21:49,084 --> 01:21:51,462
No, wait, wait. Wait. Please!

907
01:21:52,821 --> 01:21:54,892
Please don't. Please.
I don't know where they are!

908
01:21:56,158 --> 01:21:57,262
Please.

909
01:21:59,428 --> 01:22:00,702
Please!

910
01:22:01,430 --> 01:22:02,602
Please.

911
01:22:11,340 --> 01:22:12,785
I believe you're next.

912
01:22:13,375 --> 01:22:14,376
Um...

913
01:22:15,844 --> 01:22:19,121
At last, someone's acting reasonably.

914
01:22:19,615 --> 01:22:21,526
I just want a share of the reward.

915
01:22:30,459 --> 01:22:32,132
My young friend.

916
01:22:33,795 --> 01:22:35,797
You'll get your reward.

917
01:22:43,805 --> 01:22:45,148
Ten years.

918
01:22:49,211 --> 01:22:50,884
That's insulting.

919
01:22:56,985 --> 01:22:58,658
If they catch us,

920
01:23:00,489 --> 01:23:03,231
there's no way they won't
kill us, is there?

921
01:23:05,827 --> 01:23:07,329
Do you regret this?

922
01:23:08,497 --> 01:23:10,340
You saved my life.

923
01:23:12,668 --> 01:23:13,840
When?

924
01:23:15,671 --> 01:23:16,911
Now.

925
01:23:17,839 --> 01:23:19,841
And every day since I met you.

926
01:23:24,513 --> 01:23:27,255
You forget, I almost got you killed
a few times, too.

927
01:23:29,685 --> 01:23:31,858
I'm willing to overlook that.

928
01:23:48,537 --> 01:23:50,210
How's the poor little rich girl?

929
01:23:51,373 --> 01:23:52,852
I never got a chance to

930
01:23:54,042 --> 01:23:56,215
properly thank you for your time.

931
01:23:57,879 --> 01:23:59,881
I'm not surprised you stayed.

932
01:24:00,382 --> 01:24:02,726
It's the life, isn't it?

933
01:24:03,385 --> 01:24:05,729
Here we don't stop living

934
01:24:06,054 --> 01:24:08,898
until we're actually dead.

935
01:24:10,726 --> 01:24:12,501
There are a lot more ways
to die around here.

936
01:24:13,395 --> 01:24:16,399
But here, there's dancing before dying.

937
01:24:24,239 --> 01:24:27,982
Of course, it's your friend
I'm most happy to run into again.

938
01:24:28,410 --> 01:24:31,755
You've been causing a lot of trouble,
which is normally my job.

939
01:24:32,147 --> 01:24:33,353
Don't you understand?

940
01:24:34,316 --> 01:24:38,924
The reason the Timekeepers leave me alone
is 'cause I have boundaries.

941
01:24:38,987 --> 01:24:41,490
I steal from my own people.

942
01:24:42,324 --> 01:24:46,101
You surely know things are bad
when I have to restore order.

943
01:24:49,097 --> 01:24:53,273
Fortunately for you,
I don't like to kill a man in cold blood.

944
01:24:53,935 --> 01:24:55,107
I do it.

945
01:24:55,604 --> 01:24:59,279
But I prefer not to.

946
01:25:07,682 --> 01:25:09,684
I think you deserve a fighting chance.

947
01:25:16,625 --> 01:25:18,366
We play to zero.

948
01:25:19,361 --> 01:25:20,863
What's the point?

949
01:25:21,463 --> 01:25:25,138
I lose, I die. I win, they kill me.

950
01:25:26,468 --> 01:25:29,642
If you don't fight, I'll kill you now.

951
01:25:30,205 --> 01:25:31,240
And her?

952
01:25:32,641 --> 01:25:34,211
After I take you,

953
01:25:35,143 --> 01:25:36,213
I'll take her.

954
01:25:39,981 --> 01:25:42,325
Oh, yeah. And her time.

955
01:25:43,885 --> 01:25:45,455
Then I'll collect my reward

956
01:25:45,520 --> 01:25:48,000
for making everything right in the world.

957
01:27:09,938 --> 01:27:10,939
This way!

958
01:27:18,947 --> 01:27:21,120
All the time he's taken.

959
01:27:21,950 --> 01:27:23,725
Don't you mean the time
he's given away, sir?

960
01:27:26,788 --> 01:27:28,199
Even to you?

961
01:27:35,964 --> 01:27:40,811
I have given 50 years
of my life to this job.

962
01:27:41,636 --> 01:27:44,640
I am not about to see
those years go to waste.

963
01:27:46,541 --> 01:27:47,884
Goon.

964
01:28:04,392 --> 01:28:07,168
I'm sorry to be the one
to break this to you,

965
01:28:08,063 --> 01:28:09,736
but by tomorrow

966
01:28:09,998 --> 01:28:11,739
you won't have time to stand around.

967
01:28:30,352 --> 01:28:32,025
God damn it.

968
01:28:35,857 --> 01:28:37,200
It's over.

969
01:28:37,525 --> 01:28:39,436
We lost. We're not doing any good.

970
01:28:39,761 --> 01:28:41,001
At least we're trying.

971
01:28:42,030 --> 01:28:46,376
No. You don't understand. All they have to
do is keep raising the cost of living.

972
01:28:46,701 --> 01:28:50,376
A hundred years. Two. A thousand.
It does nothing.

973
01:28:50,605 --> 01:28:52,209
So, what? We just stop fighting?

974
01:28:52,440 --> 01:28:55,182
We can't win. We can't hurt them.

975
01:28:55,243 --> 01:28:57,189
The time we're taking
makes no damn difference!

976
01:28:57,245 --> 01:28:59,384
What would? What would hurt them?

977
01:28:59,948 --> 01:29:03,555
A million years.
You got a million years on you?

978
01:29:07,722 --> 01:29:10,225
I guess it really would
take a million years.

979
01:29:14,295 --> 01:29:15,569
Let's give up.

980
01:29:42,323 --> 01:29:43,666
Stop!

981
01:29:45,326 --> 01:29:46,771
I am Sylvia Weis.

982
01:29:49,097 --> 01:29:50,770
I want to surrender,

983
01:29:51,433 --> 01:29:53,071
but only to my father.

984
01:29:57,272 --> 01:29:58,808
Sylvia.

985
01:30:00,942 --> 01:30:02,421
Hello, Daddy.

986
01:30:05,246 --> 01:30:06,350
Stay where you are!

987
01:30:08,349 --> 01:30:10,625
You've hired more guards
since I last saw you.

988
01:30:10,719 --> 01:30:12,027
Thanks to you, I need them.

989
01:30:12,620 --> 01:30:13,963
One too many.

990
01:30:15,657 --> 01:30:16,897
Guns down.

991
01:30:18,460 --> 01:30:19,632
Now!

992
01:30:20,428 --> 01:30:21,429
Do it.

993
01:30:31,973 --> 01:30:33,748
Let's go for a ride.

994
01:30:41,149 --> 01:30:43,322
You'd steal from your own father.

995
01:30:43,651 --> 01:30:46,154
Is it stealing if it's already stolen?

996
01:31:00,835 --> 01:31:02,314
What's the combination?

997
01:31:03,404 --> 01:31:05,350
Well, it's not my birthday.

998
01:31:05,406 --> 01:31:08,580
You've started to regret that day,
I imagine, Father.

999
01:31:09,844 --> 01:31:12,518
Try 12-2-18-09.

1000
01:31:14,082 --> 01:31:15,857
Darwin's birthday.

1001
01:31:17,919 --> 01:31:19,694
Survival of the fittest.

1002
01:31:22,157 --> 01:31:25,070
It cost us centuries
just to bribe our way in here.

1003
01:31:25,860 --> 01:31:27,362
Let's see what it got us.

1004
01:31:44,379 --> 01:31:45,881
Quality time.

1005
01:31:47,715 --> 01:31:50,389
There really is a man with a million years.

1006
01:31:50,451 --> 01:31:53,295
That's my first million.
It won't be my last.

1007
01:31:53,388 --> 01:31:54,765
You know how much good it could do?

1008
01:31:54,789 --> 01:31:56,735
I know how much harm it could do.

1009
01:31:56,791 --> 01:31:59,601
Try to understand, even if you
gave a year to a million people,

1010
01:31:59,661 --> 01:32:01,072
you're just prolonging their agony.

1011
01:32:01,129 --> 01:32:03,075
You're prolonging their lives.

1012
01:32:03,565 --> 01:32:07,570
Flooding the wrong Zone with a million
years, it could cripple the system.

1013
01:32:07,635 --> 01:32:08,978
Let's hope so.

1014
01:32:09,070 --> 01:32:13,246
We're not meant to live like this.
We're not meant to live forever.

1015
01:32:14,142 --> 01:32:18,386
Although I do wonder, Father,
if you've ever lived a day in your life.

1016
01:32:18,913 --> 01:32:23,259
Is that so? You might upset
the balance for a generation.

1017
01:32:23,751 --> 01:32:24,923
Two.

1018
01:32:25,920 --> 01:32:28,924
But don't fool yourself.
In the end, nothing will change.

1019
01:32:29,757 --> 01:32:31,759
Because everyone wants to live forever.

1020
01:32:33,161 --> 01:32:36,074
They all think they have
a chance at immortality

1021
01:32:36,130 --> 01:32:37,850
even though all the evidence is against it.

1022
01:32:39,601 --> 01:32:41,706
They all think they will be the exception.

1023
01:32:41,769 --> 01:32:44,272
But the truth is,

1024
01:32:44,606 --> 01:32:46,745
for a few to be immortal, many must die.

1025
01:33:03,124 --> 01:33:05,968
No one should be immortal

1026
01:33:06,794 --> 01:33:09,035
if even one person has to die.

1027
01:33:23,811 --> 01:33:25,222
What was that?

1028
01:33:25,980 --> 01:33:28,483
What was that? What just happened?

1029
01:33:30,551 --> 01:33:33,631
It must be a mistake. A million years
just went off the clock in New Greenwich.

1030
01:33:33,655 --> 01:33:34,895
It's not a mistake.

1031
01:33:35,156 --> 01:33:36,200
It's gotta be a mistake, sir.

1032
01:33:36,224 --> 01:33:37,396
It's not a mistake.

1033
01:33:39,127 --> 01:33:40,197
It's them.

1034
01:33:45,166 --> 01:33:46,236
Take a month, Maurice.

1035
01:34:02,917 --> 01:34:04,954
Dispatch, what can you see?

1036
01:34:05,019 --> 01:34:06,697
<i>There's a lot of traffic
in the vicinity, sir.</i>

1037
01:34:06,721 --> 01:34:08,962
All right, look for the slowest car.

1038
01:34:10,091 --> 01:34:14,540
You have a million years.
You are definitely not in a hurry.

1039
01:34:17,198 --> 01:34:18,871
If this works...

1040
01:34:19,100 --> 01:34:21,376
If this works, we gotta get more.

1041
01:34:21,769 --> 01:34:24,443
Dayton's not the only zone that
can use a few extra years.

1042
01:34:27,208 --> 01:34:29,210
And wire me my per diem.

1043
01:34:29,277 --> 01:34:30,779
Wait. Never mind.

1044
01:34:30,878 --> 01:34:32,221
I have him.

1045
01:34:39,887 --> 01:34:41,889
Give the order, shoot on sight.

1046
01:34:41,956 --> 01:34:44,129
<i>In New Greenwich?
That's against policy, sir.</i>

1047
01:34:44,225 --> 01:34:46,466
So is having a million
years leave the Zone.

1048
01:35:04,278 --> 01:35:06,622
That time cannot leave the Zone!
Shoot on sight!

1049
01:35:31,572 --> 01:35:35,076
<i>Please deposit
one month. Please deposit one month.</i>

1050
01:35:47,688 --> 01:35:49,326
Keep going! Keep going!

1051
01:35:49,390 --> 01:35:50,460
We're close!

1052
01:35:51,025 --> 01:35:52,368
We're okay! We're okay!

1053
01:36:06,874 --> 01:36:07,909
You're late.

1054
01:36:10,311 --> 01:36:11,415
Need a minute?

1055
01:36:14,148 --> 01:36:15,559
Go. Go.

1056
01:36:16,818 --> 01:36:18,422
Where's our capsule?

1057
01:36:18,853 --> 01:36:19,991
Too late.

1058
01:36:25,493 --> 01:36:27,097
Lost a lot of time, Mr. Leon.

1059
01:36:27,495 --> 01:36:29,338
Looks like you're about out yourself.

1060
01:36:32,800 --> 01:36:34,006
- Time!
- There's time!

1061
01:36:34,068 --> 01:36:35,103
Move!

1062
01:36:52,186 --> 01:36:53,529
Move!

1063
01:36:57,525 --> 01:37:00,028
You, get out! Get out!

1064
01:37:16,210 --> 01:37:18,053
We gotta get to Livingston.

1065
01:37:19,881 --> 01:37:21,189
We can make it.

1066
01:37:21,249 --> 01:37:22,387
Can we?

1067
01:37:30,892 --> 01:37:32,064
You okay?

1068
01:37:58,819 --> 01:38:00,162
Stop!

1069
01:38:06,928 --> 01:38:08,066
You can run.

1070
01:38:10,164 --> 01:38:11,575
So can you.

1071
01:38:14,268 --> 01:38:16,077
You're from here, aren't you?

1072
01:38:18,606 --> 01:38:20,142
Long time ago.

1073
01:38:20,708 --> 01:38:21,709
Yeah.

1074
01:38:22,176 --> 01:38:24,087
I worked out how to escape.

1075
01:38:24,345 --> 01:38:26,689
And now you make sure no one else does.

1076
01:38:26,747 --> 01:38:28,283
That's the way it has to be.

1077
01:38:30,117 --> 01:38:31,960
I didn't start the clock.

1078
01:38:33,454 --> 01:38:35,092
I can't turn it back.

1079
01:38:36,624 --> 01:38:37,967
I keep it running.

1080
01:38:38,793 --> 01:38:40,101
I keep time.

1081
01:38:41,295 --> 01:38:42,968
"I keep time."

1082
01:38:47,301 --> 01:38:49,941
I'm gonna need some of that time
you borrowed from me.

1083
01:38:52,640 --> 01:38:55,712
Unless you want us to die
on the way to our execution.

1084
01:39:00,314 --> 01:39:01,657
Time.

1085
01:39:23,904 --> 01:39:25,406
We don't have enough.

1086
01:39:28,843 --> 01:39:30,914
One of us can make it. Take mine.

1087
01:39:31,178 --> 01:39:34,159
You take mine. You can get there, I can't!
I can't get there. You can.

1088
01:39:34,215 --> 01:39:36,491
- No. No.
- Yes!

1089
01:39:38,019 --> 01:39:39,191
Please.

1090
01:39:39,520 --> 01:39:40,692
No.

1091
01:39:50,364 --> 01:39:51,707
There's time.

1092
01:39:52,133 --> 01:39:54,579
- What?
- The Keeper's time. Run. Run!

1093
01:40:04,612 --> 01:40:05,955
Run!

1094
01:40:19,727 --> 01:40:20,728
I need time.

1095
01:40:20,795 --> 01:40:22,570
<i>Time transfer.</i>

1096
01:40:46,220 --> 01:40:47,563
What have we got?

1097
01:40:48,723 --> 01:40:49,997
A day.

1098
01:40:50,791 --> 01:40:52,134
Could do a lot in a day.

1099
01:41:07,641 --> 01:41:09,917
Sir, do something.

1100
01:41:11,746 --> 01:41:13,419
It's already done.

1101
01:41:14,281 --> 01:41:16,488
<i>These are
live pictures from Dayton.</i>

1102
01:41:16,550 --> 01:41:18,689
<i>Citizens have taken to the streets.</i>

1103
01:41:18,786 --> 01:41:21,289
<i>There's so much stolen time in circulation.</i>

1104
01:41:21,622 --> 01:41:23,431
<i>Fa stories in Dayton lie idle.</i>

1105
01:41:23,657 --> 01:41:25,796
<i>And now, citizens are crossing Zones,</i>

1106
01:41:25,860 --> 01:41:27,339
<i>seen here entering New Greenwich.</i>

1107
01:41:27,962 --> 01:41:30,465
<i>While authorities claim
they have the situation</i>

1108
01:41:30,531 --> 01:41:34,809
<i>under control, others fear the system
may be headed for collapse.</i>

1109
01:41:34,869 --> 01:41:37,907
<i>We will continue to update you
on this developing story.</i>

1110
01:41:38,305 --> 01:41:40,012
Sir, we lost Zone Eight.

1111
01:41:40,074 --> 01:41:41,109
And Ten.

1112
01:41:45,446 --> 01:41:47,016
It's spreading.

1113
01:41:48,682 --> 01:41:49,922
What do we do, sir?

1114
01:41:51,452 --> 01:41:52,795
Go home.

1115
01:42:01,295 --> 01:42:05,573
<i>Still no sign of
fugitives Will Salas and Sylvia Weis.</i>

1116
01:42:05,666 --> 01:42:08,237
<i>Authorities continue to ask
for the public '5 help</i>

1117
01:42:08,302 --> 01:42:11,340
<i>in bringing these criminals to justice.</i>

1118
01:42:30,391 --> 01:42:32,064
Told you there were bigger banks.

1119
01:42:33,994 --> 01:42:35,337
You almost missed your calling.

